{
  // Goods kept in stores and carried by citizens.
  // nutrition: food value per unit in percent of a standard ration (0 = not food). Grain eaten whole is poorly
  // digested; milling and baking roughly double the food a harvest provides, which is why bread chains spread.
  // targetPerCapita: how much of the good the band (later the treasury) wants per person; drives the chief's jobs.
  // value: what people first think a unit is worth, in coins (pennies). Only a starting belief: once there is a
  // market, prices come from supply and demand. Visiting merchants trade around these values ("world prices").
  // householdTarget: units a household wants to keep per member (food is counted in meals, see economy.json).
  // cpiWeight: weight in the consumer price index (the basket inflation is measured with).
